<title>UK: Courtaulds active as NatWest places stock.</title>
<headline>Courtaulds active as NatWest places stock.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in chemicals group Courtaulds Plc fell in heavy volume on Tuesday as NatWest Securities placed a line of some 10 million shares in the market at 370p, market sources said.</p>
<p>By 1253 GMT, Courtaulds shares were 8-1/2p weaker at 374-1/2 on volume of 11.7 million shares, making it the most active stock in the London market at that point.  </p>
<p>No-one at NatWest was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
